<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.5.1: Reviewing Zero Product Property</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02159</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.5.1: Reviewing Zero Product Property</md:title>
    <md:uuid>57edc9a1-c111-425d-98e4-81f790fe96e2</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Decide whether each statement is true or false.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Warm Up Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="6992756e-5681-457f-b6a7-c2e9550f74e2"><problem><para>
      <para>3 is the only solution to \(x^2−9=0\).</para>
      </para></problem><solution><para>False</para><para>
      <para>False. There are two solutions because there are two numbers that can be squared to get 9. Both 3 and –3 are possible solutions.</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
</document>
